    {
      "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
      "subContentId": "fe849809-a88e-4e00-9608-c3242a8cc79e",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "For a massless particle, what happens to the energy–momentum triangle shown above?",
        "license": "CC BY-NC-SA",
        "licenseVersion": "4.0",
        "contentType": "Multiple Choice"
      },
      "params": {
        "question": "<p>For a massless particle, what happens to the energy–momentum triangle shown above?</p>",
        "media": {
          "type": {
            "library": "H5P.Image 1.1",
            "subContentId": "0d2b1ca3-d02f-4cb4-98d0-c5e78b0a1769",
            "metadata": {
              "title": "Right triangle with legs pc and mc squared and hypotenuse E, illustrating the invariant energy–momentum relation.",
              "license": "CC BY-NC-SA",
              "licenseVersion": "4.0",
              "contentType": "Image"
            },
            "params": {
              "contentName": "Image",
              "alt": "Right triangle with legs pc and mc squared and hypotenuse E, illustrating the invariant energy–momentum relation.",
              "decorative": false,
              "file": {
                "path": "images/ch03-energy-momentum.svg",
                "mime": "image/svg+xml",
                "width": 700,
                "height": 410
              }
            }
          },
          "disableImageZooming": false
        },
        "answers": [
          {
            "text": "<div>The rest-energy leg becomes zero, so the relation reduces to E = pc.</div>",
            "correct": true,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Yes—this is one of the correct choices.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>The momentum leg becomes zero, so the relation reduces to E = mc².</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>All three sides remain nonzero and equal.</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "<div>The total-energy side becomes zero while momentum remains nonzero.</div>",
            "correct": false,
            "tipsAndFeedback": {
              "tip": "",
              "chosenFeedback": "Not this one. Revisit the chapter summary and try again.",
              "notChosenFeedback": ""
            }
          }
        ],
